{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go | sed -n '121,190p;344,390p;450,516p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go | sed -n '1422,1449p'; nl -ba .pose/adr/2026-11-22-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | sed -n '21,28p'\"","aggregated_output":"   121\t\t// case-sensitive filesystem and no tracked symlink that links a module\n   122\t\t// (other than the root) or a declared dependency with any other path.\n   123\t\tmeta, err := loadScopeMetadata(root)\n   124\t\tif err != nil {\n   125\t\t\treturn unused(\"changed-scope selection failed: %v\", err)\n   126\t\t}\n   127\t\t// Symlinks inside a submodule hide behind its gitlink (review round 8,\n   128\t\t// N20): scan each checked-out submodule at its recorded commit, and refuse\n   129\t\t// when a module or a dependency lies in one that cannot be scanned.\n   130\t\tif reason, err := submoduleAliases(root, head, modules, meta); err != nil {\n   131\t\t\treturn unused(\"submodules cannot be read: %v\", err)\n   132\t\t} else if reason != \"\" {\n   133\t\t\treturn unused(\"%s\", reason)\n   134\t\t}\n   135\t\tif link, err := aliasingSymlink(root, head, modules, meta); err != nil {\n   136\t\t\treturn unused(\"tracked symlinks cannot be read: %v\", err)\n   137\t\t} else if link != \"\" {\n   138\t\t\treturn unused(\"the tree tracks symlink %s into or out of a module or a declared dependency, so changes cannot be attributed\", link)\n   139\t\t}\n   140\t\t// A declared dependency outside the repository changes without any change\n   141\t\t// the selection can see (review round 10, N28).\n   142\t\tfor rel, module := range meta.Modules {\n   143\t\t\tfor _, dep := range module.DependsOn {\n   144\t\t\t\tclean := filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(dep))\n   145\t\t\t\tif filepath.IsAbs(dep) || path.IsAbs(clean) || clean == \"..\" || strings.HasPrefix(clean, \"../\") {\n   146\t\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"dependency %s of module %s lies outside the repository, so its changes cannot be seen\", dep, rel)\n   147\t\t\t\t}\n   148\t\t\t\t// A path that is not already clean can traverse a symlink before\n   149\t\t\t\t// its \"..\" is applied (review round 11, N30).\n   150\t\t\t\tif filepath.ToSlash(dep) != clean {\n   151\t\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"dependency %s of module %s is not a clean path, so its physical identity cannot be established\", dep, rel)\n   152\t\t\t\t}\n   153\t\t\t\t// Non-ASCII names can alias under Unicode normalization (review\n   154\t\t\t\t// round 11, N32).\n   155\t\t\t\tif !asciiPath(clean) {\n   156\t\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"dependency %s of module %s is not an ASCII path, so normalization aliases cannot be ruled out\", dep, rel)\n   157\t\t\t\t}\n   158\t\t\t}\n   159\t\t}\n   160\t\tfor _, m := range modules {\n   161\t\t\tif !asciiPath(m.Rel) {\n   162\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"module %s is not an ASCII path, so normalization aliases cannot be ruled out\", m.Rel)\n   163\t\t\t}\n   164\t\t}\n   165\t\t// Index flags that hide tracked edits from status (review round 11, N31).\n   166\t\tif hidden, err := hiddenIndexEntries(root, head); err != nil {\n   167\t\t\treturn unused(\"the index cannot be read: %v\", err)\n   168\t\t} else if hidden != \"\" {\n   169\t\t\treturn unused(\"%s is marked assume-unchanged or skip-worktree, so the working copy cannot be compared\", hidden)\n   170\t\t}\n   171\t\tif caseInsensitiveFilesystem(root, os.Stat) {\n   172\t\t\treturn unused(\"the filesystem is case-insensitive, so changes cannot be attributed to modules\")\n   173\t\t}\n   174\t\t// A case-folded directory inside a case-sensitive filesystem is an alias\n   175\t\t// too (review round 8, N22).\n   176\t\tfor _, dir := range carryRelevantDirs(root, modules, meta) {\n   177\t\t\tif casefoldedDirectory(dir, os.ReadDir, os.Lstat) {\n   178\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"directory %s folds case, so changes cannot be attributed to modules\", dir)\n   179\t\t\t}\n   180\t\t}\n   181\t\t// Check ids must be unique: two checks sharing an id would share one base\n   182\t\t// result (review round 7, N19).\n   183\t\tif id := duplicateCheckID(matrix, modules); id != \"\" {\n   184\t\t\treturn unused(\"the matrix defines check %s more than once\", id)\n   185\t\t}\n   186\t\tbaseIDs := map[string]bool{}\n   187\t\tfor _, check := range base.Checks {\n   188\t\t\tif baseIDs[check.ID] {\n   189\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"the canonical result records check %s more than once\", check.ID)\n   190\t\t\t}\n   344\t\t\t\tif dep == \".\" || p == dep || strings.HasPrefix(p, dep+\"/\") || strings.HasPrefix(dep, p+\"/\") {\n   345\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n   346\t\t\t\t}\n   347\t\t\t}\n   348\t\t\treturn false\n   349\t\t}\n   350\t\tfor _, entry := range strings.Split(string(out), \"\\x00\") {\n   351\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(entry, \"120000 \") {\n   352\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   353\t\t\t}\n   354\t\t\ttab := strings.IndexByte(entry, '\\t')\n   355\t\t\tif tab < 0 {\n   356\t\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"unexpected tree entry %q\", entry)\n   357\t\t\t}\n   358\t\t\tfields := strings.Fields(entry[:tab])\n   359\t\t\tif len(fields) != 3 {\n   360\t\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"unexpected tree entry %q\", entry)\n   361\t\t\t}\n   362\t\t\tlink := path.Join(prefix, entry[tab+1:])\n   363\t\t\tblob, err := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", repo, \"cat-file\", \"blob\", fields[2]).Output()\n   364\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   365\t\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n   366\t\t\t}\n   367\t\t\ttarget := string(blob)\n   368\t\t\tresolved := path.Clean(path.Join(path.Dir(link), target))\n   369\t\t\tif path.IsAbs(target) || resolved == \"..\" || strings.HasPrefix(resolved, \"../\") || touches(link) || touches(resolved) {\n   370\t\t\t\treturn link, nil\n   371\t\t\t}\n   372\t\t}\n   373\t\treturn \"\", nil\n   374\t}\n   375\t\n   376\t// caseInsensitiveFilesystem reports whether root's filesystem folds case: the\n   377\t// upper-case spelling of its .git entry names the same file.\n   378\tfunc caseInsensitiveFilesystem(root string, stat func(string) (os.FileInfo, error)) bool {\n   379\t\tlower, err := stat(filepath.Join(root, \".git\"))\n   380\t\tif err != nil {\n   381\t\t\treturn true\n   382\t\t}\n   383\t\tupper, err := stat(filepath.Join(root, \".GIT\"))\n   384\t\treturn err == nil && os.SameFile(lower, upper)\n   385\t}\n   386\t\n   387\t// duplicateCheckID returns a check id the matrix defines more than once.\n   388\tfunc duplicateCheckID(matrix validationMatrix, modules []validationModule) string {\n   389\t\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n   390\t\tfor _, module := range modules {\n   450\t\t\tlink, err := aliasingSymlinkIn(root, repo, commit, sub, modules, meta)\n   451\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   452\t\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n   453\t\t\t}\n   454\t\t\tif link != \"\" {\n   455\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"the tree tracks symlink %s into or out of a module or a declared dependency, so changes cannot be attributed\", link), nil\n   456\t\t\t}\n   457\t\t}\n   458\t\treturn \"\", nil\n   459\t}\n   460\t\n   461\t// carryRelevantDirs are the directories whose case behaviour decides whether\n   462\t// lexical selection is sound: every existing directory on the path from the\n   463\t// root to each module and to each declared dependency, ancestors included,\n   464\t// since any of them can fold a lookup (review round 9, N26).\n   465\tfunc carryRelevantDirs(root string, modules []validationModule, meta scopeMetadata) []string {\n   466\t\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n   467\t\tdirs := []string{}\n   468\t\tadd := func(p string) {\n   469\t\t\troot := filepath.Clean(root)\n   470\t\t\tfor p = filepath.Clean(p); ; p = filepath.Dir(p) {\n   471\t\t\t\tif p != root && !strings.HasPrefix(p, root+string(filepath.Separator)) {\n   472\t\t\t\t\treturn\n   473\t\t\t\t}\n   474\t\t\t\tif info, err := os.Stat(p); err == nil && info.IsDir() && !seen[p] {\n   475\t\t\t\t\tseen[p] = true\n   476\t\t\t\t\tdirs = append(dirs, p)\n   477\t\t\t\t}\n   478\t\t\t\tif p == root {\n   479\t\t\t\t\treturn\n   480\t\t\t\t}\n   481\t\t\t}\n   482\t\t}\n   483\t\tfor _, m := range modules {\n   484\t\t\tadd(m.Abs)\n   485\t\t}\n   486\t\tfor _, module := range meta.Modules {\n   487\t\t\tfor _, dep := range module.DependsOn {\n   488\t\t\t\tadd(filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(dep)))))\n   489\t\t\t}\n   490\t\t}\n   491\t\tsort.Strings(dirs)\n   492\t\treturn dirs\n   493\t}\n   494\t\n   495\t// casefoldedDirectory reports whether dir looks names up without case: an\n   496\t// entry spelled with its letters' case swapped names the same file.\n   497\tfunc casefoldedDirectory(dir string, readDir func(string) ([]os.DirEntry, error), stat func(string) (os.FileInfo, error)) bool {\n   498\t\t// An unreadable directory cannot be shown not to fold. Entries are probed\n   499\t\t// without following links, and an unusable one is skipped, not taken as\n   500\t\t// proof (review round 10, N27).\n   501\t\tentries, err := readDir(dir)\n   502\t\tif err != nil {\n   503\t\t\treturn true\n   504\t\t}\n   505\t\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n   506\t\t\tname := entry.Name()\n   507\t\t\tswapped := swapCase(name)\n   508\t\t\tif swapped == name {\n   509\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   510\t\t\t}\n   511\t\t\toriginal, err := stat(filepath.Join(dir, name))\n   512\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   513\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   514\t\t\t}\n   515\t\t\t// The first usable entry decides: its swapped spelling names the same\n   516\t\t\t// file only where lookups fold case.\n  1422\t\trun.WallSeconds = time.Since(wallStart).Seconds()\n  1423\t\t// A check that changed a tracked file changed the material it ran over: the\n  1424\t\t// committed tree no longer describes what was validated.\n  1425\t\tendedClean := materialTrackedUnchanged(root)\n  1426\t\t// The run validated its recorded head only if HEAD never moved: a commit\n  1427\t\t// made while checks ran would let them observe code the record does not\n  1428\t\t// name (review round 4, N10).\n  1429\t\tendHead := \"\"\n  1430\t\tif head, err := gitOutputBounded(root, 1024, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"); err == nil {\n  1431\t\t\tendHead = strings.TrimSpace(string(head))\n  1432\t\t}\n  1433\t\t// Untracked material created while checks ran counts too (review round 8,\n  1434\t\t// N21): only ignored files may differ from the recorded head.\n  1435\t\thidden, hiddenErr := hiddenIndexEntries(root, run.GitHead)\n  1436\t\trun.MaterialClean = startedClean && endedClean && materialWorktreeClean(root) && run.GitHead != \"\" && endHead == run.GitHead && hiddenErr == nil && hidden == \"\"\n  1437\t\t// A run that did not validate its recorded head binds no material: its\n  1438\t\t// bindings would let a later tree make a misattributed pass current again\n  1439\t\t// (review round 5, N12).\n  1440\t\tif len(run.MaterialProvenance) > 0 && !run.MaterialClean {\n  1441\t\t\tfor spec := range run.MaterialProvenance {\n  1442\t\t\t\trun.MaterialProvenance[spec] = posemodel.MaterialBindingUnavailable\n  1443\t\t\t}\n  1444\t\t}\n  1445\t\t// A cancelled run never reads as a success, whatever the severity of the\n  1446\t\t// checks it stopped (review round 1, B5).\n  1447\t\tcancelled := false\n  1448\t\tfor _, check := range run.Checks {\n  1449\t\t\tcancelled = cancelled || check.LimitState == \"cancelled\"\n    21\tA module may declare `\"selfContained\": true` in its metadata. A change outside every module then stops selecting it. The declaration is the instance's statement that the module's checks read only its own directory and its declared dependencies, so it applies to `--changed-from` too. Without it, the existing safe fallback stays.\n    22\t\n    23\t## Consequences\n    24\t\n    25\tA change confined to one module reruns that module, the modules enclosing it (the root module included), the modules beneath the changed path and its declared dependents. Everything else is reused with its true origin visible. Only a changed file that no module owns widens the run to every module that does not declare itself self-contained. Consumers that compare a result's head with a subject head now see carried results as observations of the earlier head, which is accurate. An incorrect `selfContained` declaration can carry a stale result. That risk sits with the instance's explicit declaration and is documented next to it.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Alternatives considered\n    28\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
