{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"diff -u POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md | head -30; git status --porcelain; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | sed -n '198,207p'\"","aggregated_output":"--- POSE.md\t2026-11-23 06:32:31.979285237 -0300\n+++ pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\t2026-11-23 06:32:32.019449745 -0300\n@@ -574,19 +574,6 @@\n - assisted execution via [`pose`](pose) (CLI)\n - progressive maturity with skills in [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/)\n \n-## Open-Source POSE Contributor Mode\n-\n-<!-- pose:contributor-mode -->\n-\n-This repository has enabled POSE Contributor Mode. Executing AI agents collaborate on improving POSE engine stability and developer experience under explicit user adjudication.\n-\n-- **Continuous Opportunity Scouting**: On every issue resolution or task execution, proactively scout for related improvements, edge cases, root-level parity gaps, or complementary corrections across adjacent tools and commands.\n-- **User Consent & Explicit Adjudication**: Staging or submitting contributions upstream is ALWAYS an explicit user decision. Agents must ask the user for confirmation before staging drafts under `.pose/contributions/` or opening GitHub issues.\n-- **Lifecycle & Status Integrity**: Track contribution states (`staged` -> `submitted` / `dismissed`) with `pose contribute list --status <staged|submitted|dismissed|all>`, `pose contribute submit <file>`, `pose contribute mark-submitted <file> [--issue-url <url>]`, or `pose contribute dismiss <file>`.\n-- Check contributor status: `pose contribute status`\n-- Stage a contribution manually: `pose contribute stage --type <bug|enhancement> --title <title>`\n-- Disable contributor mode: `pose contribute disable`\n-- Privacy guarantee: staged reports strictly isolate POSE engine mechanics and never leak proprietary code.\n ## Opt-in progressive review profiles (ABM)\n \n Add `engineering-judgment@1` and/or `high-criticality-review@1` explicitly to\n   198\t\n   199\t### Results summary\n   200\tAll new and existing tests pass, and the strict matrix is green. In this repository, `pose-mcp` holds 233 of the 236 checks and is high criticality, so carrying saves little here. In an instance with many modules, a change confined to one of them reruns that module, the modules enclosing it and its declared dependents. A changed file that no module owns also reruns every module that is not declared self-contained.\n   201\t\n   202\t### Requirement trace\n   203\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestCarryRefusesIncompatibleFlags\n   204\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun test:TestCarryRefusesAFilteredBase test:TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy test:TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds test:TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink test:TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean test:TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunBindsNoMaterial test:TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory test:TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead test:TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink test:TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule test:TestCarryRefusesASymlinkFromAModuleToAnUnownedPath test:TestCarryAllowsSymlinksBetweenUnownedPaths test:TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem test:TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs test:TestValidateUntrackedMaterialCreatedDuringTheRunIsNotClean test:TestCarryRefusesAnAliasingSymlinkInsideASubmodule test:TestCarryDetectsACaseFoldedDirectory test:TestCarryScansAGitlinkInsideAModule test:TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor test:TestCarryCaseProbeSkipsUnusableEntries test:TestCarryRefusesDependenciesOutsideTheRepository test:TestCarryRefusesUncleanDependencies test:TestCarryRefusesNonASCIIPaths test:TestCarryRefusesHiddenIndexEntries\n   205\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestCarryRunsOnlyTheChangedModule test:TestCarryRecordFileIsNotAChange test:TestCarryIgnoresDerivedAdministrativeRecords test:TestCarrySelectsAModuleWithoutAPriorResult\n   206\t- R4 [satisfied] test:TestCarryKeepsTheOriginalHeadAcrossChainedCarries test:TestCarryKeepsACarriedFailureAFailure\n   207\t- R5 [satisfied] test:TestCarryRunsOnlyTheChangedModule\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"The sweep found a third blocker in the case-folding probe: its first filename can produce a false negative. For example, Unicode case folding keeps dotless `ı` distinct from `I`, while the probe swaps `ı` to `I`; it can therefore miss an ancestor that aliases ASCII `a` and `A`.\n\nThe strict module run failed because the sandbox denied temporary build writes. I’ll report that separately from the sealed green matrix. The checkout is still unchanged.\n"}}
