{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nPrior findings:\n\n| ID | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| R8-N26 | fixed | `carryRelevantDirs` now walks every ancestor: `validate_carry.go:465–492`; targeted regression passed. |\n| R9-N27 | fixed | The probe uses `Lstat`, skips unusable entries, and refuses unreadable directories: `validate_carry.go:497–513`; targeted regression passed. |\n| R9-N28 | fixed | Absolute and escaping dependencies refuse carry: `validate_carry.go:145–146`; targeted regression passed. |\n| R9-N29 | fixed | Corrected ADR consequences at line 25 and spec results summary at line 200. |\n\nThree remaining defects, all **high / blocker**:\n\n1. **R12-N33 — Ignored symlinks bypass dependency alias detection.**  \n   `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:135` checks tracked symlinks only. With an ignored `link -> a` and self-contained `b` declaring `dependsOn:[\"link/input\"]`, a committed change to `a/input` selects `a` but misses `b`. The dependency is clean and ASCII, status remains clean, and no guard resolves its physical identity. Consequently, `b` can carry a stale pass while reading its explicitly declared dependency. Resolve dependency paths and their existing ancestors physically, including ignored symlinks. Established by source trace; scratch reproduction was unavailable.\n\n2. **R12-N34 — Returning HEAD to its starting commit hides intervening movement.**  \n   `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1436` compares only the starting and ending commits. If another process changes `H → H′`, a check observes the fixed input at `H′`, and HEAD returns to `H` before completion, `material_clean` remains true. The pass and material bindings are attributed to `H` and become eligible for carry. This violates R2’s requirement that HEAD did not move during validation. Validate an immutable checkout or otherwise detect intervening changes. Established by source trace; this sequence was not newly executed.\n\n3. **R12-N35 — The first Unicode filename can conceal case folding.**  \n   `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:518` returns after its first usable entry. In a Unicode case-folded directory, an entry `0ı` swaps to `0I`, but those names need not alias; ASCII `a` and `A` still do. Thus, a folded `shared` directory containing `0ı` and a case-sensitive child `shared/a` can pass the probe. With modules `shared/a` and `b`, and `b` depending on ASCII path `shared/A/input`, changing `shared/a/input` can carry `b`. The ASCII guards do not constrain probe entries. Use a probe whose negative result establishes the required lookup behavior. Established by source trace and Python’s Unicode case-fold model; matching filesystem hardware was not exercised.\n\nTargeted carry/selection tests, the delivery-reader test, and `go vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose` passed. The module-wide strict run failed because the sandbox denied temporary build writes; the full strict run was also attempted but did not complete during this review. Sealed matrix evidence remains green. Assessment commands were omitted because scratch creation was denied and those commands persist files. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\nRules applied: POSE review workflow, backend Go, security, documentation style, and delivery evidence. The structural ADR maps to D1–D3. The sweep covered all changed runtime files, tests, docs/scaffolds, selection and dependency widening, submodules, aliases, engine identity, metadata, chained carries, cancellation, and canonical publication.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N33\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 135,\n      \"summary\": \"Dependency aliases through ignored symlinks escape the tracked-tree guard. With ignored link -> a and self-contained b depending on link/input, changing tracked a/input selects a but can carry b's stale pass. The dependency loop checks spelling and confinement but never resolves its physical identity. Resolve dependency paths and existing ancestors, including ignored symlinks. Established by source inspection; no new filesystem fixture was possible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N34\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1436,\n      \"summary\": \"Endpoint equality does not establish that HEAD never moved. A concurrent H -> H-prime -> H transition can let checks observe H-prime while material_clean stays true and material bindings remain available for H. That result becomes an eligible carry base despite R2. Validate immutable material or detect intervening movement. Established by source inspection; the concurrent sequence was not newly executed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N35\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 518,\n      \"summary\": \"The first usable filename can falsely establish case sensitivity. Unicode dotless i swaps to I but does not have the same Unicode case fold, so first entry 0ı can return false in a directory that aliases ASCII a/A. A folded shared ancestor with case-sensitive child shared/a, module b depending on shared/A/input, and a change to shared/a/input can therefore carry b. ASCII module/dependency checks do not constrain probe entries. Established by source inspection and a Python Unicode case-fold model; matching filesystem hardware was not exercised.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N26\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:465-492 walks all dependency/module ancestors; TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor passed in the targeted carry test run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R9-N27\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:497-513 refuses unreadable directories and skips unusable Lstat entries; TestCarryCaseProbeSkipsUnusableEntries passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R9-N28\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:145-146 refuses absolute and root-escaping dependencies; TestCarryRefusesDependenciesOutsideTheRepository passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R9-N29\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/adr/2026-11-22-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:25 and .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:200 now correctly distinguish module-owned changes from the unowned-file fallback.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the complete declared implementation and documentation diff against R1-R10 and D1-D3. Swept argument restrictions, eligibility, metadata decoding, matrix and engine identity, moduleOverrides without manifests, nested/root ownership, dependency and criticality widening, rename and quoted paths, gitlinks and submodules, symlinks and ignored aliases, ASCII/Unicode and case-fold lookup, hidden index entries, chained origins, outcomes/counts, cancellation, material binding lifecycle, concurrent HEAD movement, canonical publication locking/atomicity, delivery consumers, and English/Portuguese scaffold parity. Read the adversarial corpus; the reported alias and temporal shortcuts have no corresponding enforced case. Targeted tests and vet passed. Strict module validation failed on read-only temporary-build writes; full validation was attempted but remained incomplete. Persistent assessments could not run on a scratch copy because scratch creation was denied. Repository status remained clean.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R12-N33\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The explicit selfContained declaration is documented, but declared dependency identity is still an unresolved assumption when ignored symlinks are present.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R12-N34\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected additive result fields, CLI restrictions, old-record fallback, and delivery parsing. Records without carry fields retain their previous head/time interpretation; unstamped old bases are refused.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R12-N35\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R12-N33\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 requires unchanged inputs before assigning current material bindings to reused observations. The lexical selection and tracked-only alias guard do not establish that premise.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records carrying an earlier observation with its original head, conservative eligibility, and the selfContained declaration; D2 and D3 supply the matrix/engine and fallback decisions.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R12-N34\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Manual and scaffold describe material_clean as proving HEAD did not move during the run, while runtime checks only endpoint equality.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R12-N33\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Recognized eligibility failures have actionable reasons, but the ignored-alias case silently reports successful reuse without warning or remediation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R12-N34\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-afbff5faaf07e873\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Changes are confined to canonical carry eligibility, shared changed-scope selection, result origins, tests, ADR, help, and distributed manuals, as declared by the spec.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R12-N33\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision confinement and raw-history Git helpers are preserved, but the dependency authority boundary can alias an unselected input through an ignored symlink.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-afbff5faaf07e873\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the selected module-level carry design with full reruns and per-check input hashing. Reusing existing selection and additive origins is proportionate and avoids a speculative input-declaration system. Its suitability depends on conservative refusal whenever input identity cannot be established; the reported defects must close that boundary.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Command exited 0. It reported 15 claims, 20 observations, and broader provenance warnings; its trailer-resolved range extends beyond the sealed subject, consistent with the disclosed attribution behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed sealed structure:design-afbff5faaf07e873 and inspected the ADR directly. No assessment was run in the sealed checkout; scratch creation was denied.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment persists files. Both /tmp and operation-scratch directory creation were denied by the read-only sandbox.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment persists files and no writable scratch copy could be created. Inspected delivery boundaries and used sealed integration evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment persists files and scratch creation was denied. Reviewed changed implementation directly without modifying assessment or state records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires the completed review conclusion; no attestation was recorded, as instructed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires the completed review conclusion; no attestation was recorded, as instructed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules and the review workflow.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Attempted pose validate --strict; the independent full invocation did not complete during this review. The cited sealed canonical unit result passed, as did the sealed build/integration/e2e matrix; this is not a claim that the independent full invocation passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp; it exited 1 with 233 failed steps because temporary Go build and cache writes were denied by the read-only sandbox. The cited sealed canonical result passed. Separate targeted carry/selection tests, delivery-reader test, and go vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
